"notices":{"DATASET_CARD.md":"# Thereabouts golden v2\n\nVerified country-checkpointed city normalization at H3 resolution 8.\n6,875,329 places; 68,923 absorbing cities/towns; 66,226,680 compact cells.\n\nCountry/state/land membership retains the base snapshot. Policy polygons, accepted city polygons, GHSL urban allocation and optional town radii precede rural polygons/nearest settlements. Nearest answers beyond 25 km are flagged; 50 km remains the inclusive cutoff.\n\nSee quality.json and quality/<country>.json for regenerated checks, including failures; these consistency/source checks are not independent accuracy. Dhaka has an inferred urban allocation, not a verified municipal boundary. See docs/GOLDEN_V2.md for reproduction and limitations.\n","DATA_LICENSES.md":"# Golden dataset attribution and licence summary (draft)\n\nKeep every row's original licence and provenance. This is a combined derivative\ndatabase, not a relicensing of its inputs. Review distribution obligations before\npublishing this draft, including attribution and database share-alike terms.\n\n| Input | Recorded terms / required attribution |\n| --- | --- |\n| OpenStreetMap land | ODbL 1.0; © OpenStreetMap contributors, https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright |\n| Overture divisions | ODbL 1.0; Overture Maps Foundation, OpenStreetMap and the upstream sources retained in provenance |\n| GeoNames places and postal | CC BY 4.0; GeoNames, https://www.geonames.org/; GB postal also retains Royal Mail copyright/database-right 2022 |\n| geoBoundaries | Per-layer licences in reconciliation provenance; the policy only admits its explicit compatible-licence list |\n| Country / subdivision codes | DataHub PDDL 1.0; GeoNames CC BY 4.0; iso-codes/pycountry LGPL 2.1 or later |\n| OurAirports | Public domain; https://ourairports.com/data/ |\n| UN/LOCODE | UNECE / DataHub, PDDL 1.0; source identifies edition 2024.2.0 |\n| Timezones | timezone-boundary-builder and OpenStreetMap, ODbL 1.0; IANA tables public domain |\n| Phone | Google libphonenumber, Apache 2.0 |\n| DB-IP Lite | CC BY 4.0; “IP Geolocation by DB-IP”, https://db-ip.com |\n\nSource URLs, releases, original notices, identity and boundary evidence remain\nin the acquired manifests, reconciled partitions and golden provenance columns.\n\n## GHSL\n\nCC BY 4.0. European Commission, Joint Research Centre (JRC), GHS-UCDB R2024A; Pesaresi et al. (2024), Advances on the Global Human Settlement Layer by joint assessment of Earth Observation and population survey data, International Journal of Digital Earth 17(1). https://doi.org/10.1080/17538947.2024.2390454\n\nhttps://human-settlement.emergency.copernicus.eu/GHSLhowToCite.php\nWGS84 conversion and city allocation are modifications.\n"},"sources":["golden dataset; original digests retained"]},"writer":"0.3.3"},"sources":["golden dataset; original digests retained"],"attribution":"GeoNames and golden context sources; see notices","files":[{"path":"records-00000.bin","kind":"records","size":235,"sha256":"67e0b3fc21cff4aad7fe0bea54c53c468cc3faaef4336adb756ca8a6c313bc2f"},{"path":"evidence-00000.bin","kind":"evidence","size":481,"sha256":"df7889e5d0f069ace80aa927d0d67dbab744a723971265cf69a80de69ce0f66e"},{"path":"keys.bin","kind":"keys","size":14384,"sha256":"5bc2b9c070c77e71c354856dfd4b32cc24ee95d3bfc1359e68d23332dde9b696"},{"path":"strings-00000.bin","kind":"strings","size":153,"sha256":"58a03e87fdd1c3888706c108ee4a3f4a6c2696c715a154e00e6804f6dda71c7a"},{"path":"evidence_strings-00000.bin","kind":"evidence_strings","size":52292,"sha256":"95b5c52bf275b9bc50dfd5ad1c2b6b71dffd4f715726c2fd82042488fbab9c1a"},{"path":"geographies-00000.bin","kind":"geographies","size":6507,"sha256":"4e76d9183e4e7088de6a2eb193e5ba397da916a31ab7e94a8d780daecc2fba98"},{"path":"locations-00000.bin","kind":"locations","size":24902,"sha256":"9ff8468babd0592802ad12b61cd6b2b33a57b60b206c42d0a6d7807b0a20cbd2"},{"path":"details-00000.bin","kind":"details","size":14889,"sha256":"c2a6b062fb0e4fb901072ef808